FORMAT 1
SCENARIO Branches and merging
LABEL    Bonus
SUMMARY  git switch -c, work on a branch, git merge and a merge commit with two parents.
INTRO    You want to try new recipes in the cookbook without breaking the main version. That is what **branches** are for.

SETUP
  PERSON jana NAME "Jana Nováková" EMAIL "novakovaj@jirovcovka.net" LOGIN "jana-novakova" LABEL "Jana's computer"
  MACHINE jana CONFIGURED
  REPOSITORY git/cookbook
  PS> mkdir git
  PS> cd git
  PS> mkdir cookbook
  PS> cd cookbook
  PS> git init
  FILE pancakes.md
    # Pancakes

    ## Ingredients

    - 250 ml milk
    - 1 egg
    - 120 g plain flour
    - a pinch of salt

    ## Tip

    I fill them with strawberry jam.
  END
  PS> git add .
  PS> git commit -m "Add pancake recipe"
  FILE README.md
    # My cookbook

    My favourite recipes.
  END
  PS> git add .
  PS> git commit -m "Add README"
  VSCODE git/cookbook
END

TASK Create a branch **new-recipes** and switch to it.
  HINT  git switch -c new-recipes
  HINT  git branch
  CHECK branch new-recipes exists
END

TASK On the branch, create **drop-scones.md** and commit it.
  HINT  git add drop-scones.md
  HINT  git commit -m "Add drop scones"
  CHECK file drop-scones.md in branch new-recipes exists
END

TASK Switch back to **main**. What happened to the file **drop-scones.md**?
  HINT  git switch main
  CHECK on branch main
  CHECK command "git switch main" was run
END

TASK On **main**, edit the README and commit. The history splits in two – look at the graph.
  HINT  git commit -am "Update README"
  HINT  git log --oneline --graph --all
  CHECK branches main and new-recipes have diverged
END

TASK Merge the branch **new-recipes** into **main**. Leave the message in MERGE_MSG as it is.
  HINT     git merge new-recipes
  HINT     git log --oneline --graph
  QUESTION How many parents does the merge commit have?
  CHECK    on branch main
  CHECK    HEAD is a merge
END
